      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T21:26:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d really like to avoid this complexity, if possible.\n\nCould we try removing all the round-to-16s, and see what breaks? I honestly can\u0027t remember why I added it. I don\u0027t think the interior padding (a struct member embedded in another struct) can actually be different between GLSL and WGSL, since otherwise, the layout provided by the host would have to be different. But if GLSL truly does require tail padding, then it\u0027s different than WGSL and this complexity is justified.",
      "revId": "f53e75db4e399dfb106dd58e0a21d41417279d37",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f640c9f5_26940c23",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000024
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-07T21:30:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s the original CL: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/101720\n\nSadly, I didn\u0027t mention why rounding up for struct members was necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "27f3ec32_148b04ec",
      "revId": "f53e75db4e399dfb106dd58e0a21d41417279d37",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e1798c2_b459d697",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000685
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-10T01:40:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this roundding up uniform struct size to 16-byte:https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/e77f22682b24771fc167d2a03595c2e7db7c54a0:third_party/dawn/src/tint/lang/glsl/writer/ast_raise/pad_structs.cc;l\u003d128\n\nis to satisfy this wgsl validation: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/e77f22682b24771fc167d2a03595c2e7db7c54a0:third_party/dawn/src/tint/lang/wgsl/resolver/validator.cc;l\u003d644\n\n\"uniform storage requires that the number of bytes between the start of the \"\n\"previous member of type struct and the current member be a \"\n\"multiple of 16 bytes...\"\n\nexample:\n```\nerror: \u0027uniform\u0027 storage requires that the number of bytes between the start of the previous member of type struct and the current member be a multiple of 16 bytes, but there are currently 12 bytes between \u0027tint_symbol_5\u0027 and \u0027tint_symbol_3\u0027. Consider setting \u0027@align(16)\u0027 on this member\n:8:8 note: see layout of struct:\n/*            align(4) size(44) */ struct tint_symbol_4 {\n/* offset( 0) align(4) size( 4) */   tint_symbol_1 : u32,\n/* offset( 4) align(4) size( 4) */   pad : u32,\n/* offset( 8) align(4) size( 4) */   pad_1 : u32,\n/* offset(12) align(4) size( 4) */   pad_2 : u32,\n/* offset(16) align(4) size(12) */   tint_symbol_5 : tint_symbol,\n/* offset(28) align(4) size( 4) */   tint_symbol_3 : u32,\n/* offset(32) align(4) size( 4) */   pad_3 : u32,\n/* offset(36) align(4) size( 4) */   pad_4 : u32,\n/* offset(40) align(4) size( 4) */   pad_5 : u32,\n/*                              */ };\n```\n\nThis seems to be a wgsl restrction but not a glsl std140 restriction. (size of a struct in glsl doesn\u0027t need to be multiple of 16; offset of a struct member inside a block needs to be multiple of 16)\n\nSo I tried instead of add padding in the wgsl transform, adding @size attribute with a size round up to 16.\n\nThis passed the ComputeLayoutMemoryBufferTests.StructMember tests on android pixel 6.\n\nHopefully this should work. CL: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/201816",
      "parentUuid": "f640c9f5_26940c23",
      "revId": "f53e75db4e399dfb106dd58e0a21d41417279d37",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
