      "writtenOn": "2024-08-14T19:19:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@align(12) seems like it would violate this:\n\nIf align(n) is applied to a member of S with type T, and S is the store type or contained in the store type for a variable in address space C, then n must satisfy: n \u003d k × RequiredAlignOf(T,C) for some positive integer k.\n\n(Where RequiredAlignOf(T, C) is 16 for a struct in a uniform block.)",
      "parentUuid": "c00c4000_4d59627f",
      "revId": "f53e75db4e399dfb106dd58e0a21d41417279d37",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
