      "message": "```\n// input\nstruct A {\n  x: u32;\n  y: u32;\n  z: u32;\n};\nstruct B {\n  x : u32,\n  @align(16)\n  a : A,\n};\nstruct S {\n  @size(16)  // this needs updating\n  b: B\n}\n```\n\nI\u0027m confused. If this is the input, how does `@size(16)` pass validation *before* the pad_structs transform? `B` must be 32 bytes, no? (Even as a storage buffer, it would be 28, which is \u003e16.)",
