      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I hand typed the test case and may be incorrect.\n\nHere is the example I used in test now\n\n- input:\n\n```\nstruct A {\n  @size(32i)\n  x : u32,\n}\n\nstruct B {\n  @size(64i)\n  x : A,\n  y : u32,\n}\n\nstruct U {\n  @align(16) @size(80)\n  b : B,\n}\n```\n\n- output:\n\n```\n@internal(disable_validation__ignore_struct_member)\nstruct A {\n  x : u32,\n  pad : u32,\n  pad_1 : u32,\n  pad_2 : u32,\n  pad_3 : u32,\n  pad_4 : u32,\n  pad_5 : u32,\n  pad_6 : u32,\n}\n\n@internal(disable_validation__ignore_struct_member)\nstruct B {\n  @align(16) @size(64)\n  x : A,\n  pad : u32,\n  pad_1 : u32,\n  pad_2 : u32,\n  pad_3 : u32,\n  pad_4 : u32,\n  pad_5 : u32,\n  pad_6 : u32,\n  pad_7 : u32,\n  y : u32,\n}\n\n@internal(disable_validation__ignore_struct_member)\nstruct U {\n  @align(16) @size(80)\n  b : B,\n}\n```\n\n\n@size(80) needs updating now (now size B is 112)",
